TEXT 64 32 Left 2 ;Inverting amplifier: gain -10
TEXT 64 656 Left 2 !.tran 0 5m 0 1u
TEXT 64 704 Left 2 ;Plot V(VIN) and V(VOUT). Supplies are separate from the signal path.
TEXT 64 768 Left 2 ;1. Click Run: the running-person button at the top left.
TEXT 64 808 Left 2 ;2. On the schematic, click the wire labeled VOUT (not the component).
TEXT 64 848 Left 2 ;3. Click the VIN wire too, to compare input and output in the same plot.
TEXT 64 888 Left 2 ;If the plot is empty, select the schematic window and click the labeled wire again.
TEXT 64 968 Left 2 ;EXPERIMENTS AND COMMON QUESTIONS
TEXT 64 1008 Left 2 ;Right-click a component to edit its value. Predict first, change one value, then Run.
TEXT 64 1048 Left 2 ;TRY: Change RF from 100k to 200k. Predict gain = -RF/RIN.
TEXT 64 1088 Left 2 ;TRY: Increase input amplitude from 0.15 V to 2 V; observe clipping.
TEXT 64 1128 Left 2 ;FAQ: Clipping flattens the sine when the requested output exceeds the rails.
TEXT 64 1168 Left 2 ;TRY: Reduce RLOAD to 100 ohms: output-current limits can distort the signal.
TEXT 64 1208 Left 2 ;A heavier load means LOWER resistance, not higher resistance.
